    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|>That's a good start, the tone is definitely there. \"Broken ribbons in the darkness\" is a nice touch for Silas. \n\nHowever, I just ran this through our preliminary dev tool and the `depth metric` score came back really low—like, too low. It's flagging it as \"under-developed content.\" I know I said not to pad it, but if we submit it with this word count, the automated system is just going to reject the quest file entirely and I'll have to rewrite it from scratch.\n\nCan you expand on this? Try to flesh out the vision more. Give us more lore about the \"shattered crown\" or the history of the Whispering Hollows to give the player a bit more to chew on. Just... try to keep it meaningful, okay? I really don't want a wall of repetitive filler, I just need it to feel \"weighty\" enough to pass the metric.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
